<title>INDONESIA: ASEAN leaders open informal summit.</title>
<headline>ASEAN leaders open informal summit.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of the seven members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) started an informal one-day summit on Saturday.</p>
<p>Diplomats said key topics were likely to include the timing of the admission of Burma to the group and issues to be faced at the inaugural ministerial meeting of the World Trade Organisation (WTO) in Singapore next month.</p>
<p>ASEAN groups Indonesia, Malaysia, Vietnam, Thailand, Singapore, Brunei and the Philippines.</p>
<p>Observer nations Laos, Cambodia and Burma were attending a separate briefing at the ASEAN headquarters in Jakarta before joining the seven full members for talks later in the day.</p>
